<div class="landing landing-home">
  <div class="home-top">
    <.marketing_nav current_user={assigns[:current_user]} />

    <section class="home-hero home-hero-compact">
      <div class="home-wrap">
        <p class="home-eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="home-lede">Last updated 12 October 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="home-band">
    <div class="home-wrap">
      <div class="legal">
        <p>
          This policy explains which personal data Masthead collects, why, who receives it and
          what you can do about it. It covers masthead.site, the Masthead dashboard and the
          sites Masthead hosts.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Masthead is provided by <strong>Dijkstra Software</strong>, a sole proprietorship
          registered in the Netherlands with the Chamber of Commerce (KvK) under number
          97259993. We are the controller for the personal data described here. For any
          privacy question or request, email <a href="mailto:hello@masthead.site">hello@masthead.site</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Data</th>
              <th>Purpose</th>
              <th>Legal basis</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Account: email address, a hashed password (never the password itself), or your
                Google or GitHub account identifier when you sign in with one
              </td>
              <td>Creating your account and signing you in</td>
              <td>Contract</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Your sites: content, uploads, settings, themes and collaborators</td>
              <td>Hosting and publishing your sites</td>
              <td>Contract</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Billing: plan, status, period end, and Stripe customer and subscription
                identifiers. Card details go to Stripe and never reach us.
              </td>
              <td>Selling and managing site licenses</td>
              <td>Contract, and legal obligations for tax records</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Account email: confirmation, password reset and security messages</td>
              <td>Running your account</td>
              <td>Contract</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Product email: tips and updates to people who created a site. Every message has
                an unsubscribe link, and you can switch it off in your account settings.
              </td>
              <td>Helping you get started and telling you about Masthead</td>
              <td>Legitimate interest</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Signup source: the campaign tags in the link you arrived through, whether it came
                from an ad click, the first page you visited, the referring website's domain and
                the time of that first visit. Never your IP address or the ad click identifier
                itself.
              </td>
              <td>Learning which channels bring people who use Masthead</td>
              <td>Legitimate interest</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>
                Usage: the days on which you did something in the dashboard (such as writing,
                publishing or changing settings), and when you first published
              </td>
              <td>Understanding activation and retention, in aggregate</td>
              <td>Legitimate interest</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Support chat: the messages you send and any email address you give</td>
              <td>Answering your questions</td>
              <td>Contract or legitimate interest</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Google Analytics and Google Ads measurement</td>
              <td>Measuring visits and which ads lead to signups</td>
              <td>Consent (see <a href="#cookies">Cookies</a>)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>Visitors of sites hosted on Masthead</h2>
        <p>
          Sites on Masthead count page views and daily unique visitors without cookies. To
          count a visitor once per day, we combine a secret key, the date, the site, the
          visitor's IP address and browser identifier into a one-way hash. The IP address and
          browser identifier are never stored, the hash changes every day so visits on
          different days can't be linked, and the hashes are deleted after a day. Only daily
          totals are kept, for one year. Known bots are not counted.
        </p>
        <p>
          The owner of a site decides what it publishes and is responsible for any personal
          data in its content and forms. For that data, Masthead processes it on the site
          owner's behalf.
        </p>

        <h2>Who receives data</h2>
        <p>We use these service providers, each only for the purpose listed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Fly.io</strong>: hosting of the application and database</li>
          <li><strong>Tigris</strong>: storage of uploaded files</li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong>: sending email, and the contact list for product email</li>
          <li><strong>Stripe</strong>: payments and subscriptions</li>
          <li><strong>Chatwoot</strong>: the support chat</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google</strong>: sign-in with Google if you choose it, and Google
            Analytics and Google Ads measurement if you consent
          </li>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong>: sign-in with GitHub if you choose it</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some of these providers are based in, or process data in, the United States. Where
          data leaves the European Economic Area, the transfer relies on the EU–US Data Privacy
          Framework or the European Commission's standard contractual clauses. We don't sell
          personal data.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Account, site and usage data: for as long as your account exists.</li>
          <li>
            Accounts whose email address is never confirmed are suspended after 30 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            After you ask us to delete your account, we delete it and its sites within 30 days.
            Copies in backups disappear when those backups expire.
          </li>
          <li>Billing records: seven years, as Dutch tax law requires.</li>
          <li>Site visitor statistics: daily totals for one year; visitor hashes for one day.</li>
          <li>The signup source cookie: 30 days, or until you sign up.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Masthead uses a few cookies of its own that the service needs, and Google's cookies
          only if you accept them in the cookie banner.
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Name</th>
              <th>Set by</th>
              <th>Purpose</th>
              <th>Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_masthead_key</code></td>
              <td>Masthead</td>
              <td>Keeps you signed in and protects forms. Essential.</td>
              <td>Session</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_mh_attr</code></td>
              <td>Masthead</td>
              <td>
                Remembers how you first arrived, for the signup source above. First-party, never
                shared, no IP address.
              </td>
              <td>30 days, removed at signup</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>masthead_no_track</code></td>
              <td>Masthead</td>
              <td>Keeps a site's own members out of its visitor statistics</td>
              <td>7 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>cw_conversation</code> and similar</td>
              <td>Chatwoot</td>
              <td>Keeps your support conversation open between pages</td>
              <td>Set by Chatwoot</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td>
              <td>Google Analytics</td>
              <td>Counts visits and how people use the site. Only with your consent.</td>
              <td>Up to 2 years</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_gcl_*</code></td>
              <td>Google Ads</td>
              <td>Links signups to ad clicks. Only with your consent.</td>
              <td>Up to 90 days</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          Your cookie choice is stored in your browser's local storage. If you decline, Google
          may still receive cookieless signals, such as that a page was viewed or that a signup
          happened, without any cookie or identifier on your device; Google uses these only for
          aggregate measurement.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" data-consent-open>
            Change your cookie choice
          </button>
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask for a copy of your personal data, have it corrected or deleted, restrict
          or object to its use, receive it in a portable format, and withdraw consent at any
          time. Email <a href="mailto:hello@masthead.site">hello@masthead.site</a>; we answer
          within one month. You can also complain to the Dutch data protection authority, the <a
            href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
          >
          Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</a>, or the authority where you live.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>You must be at least 16 to create a Masthead account.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          When this policy changes, the date at the top changes too. We email account holders
          about significant changes before they take effect.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <.marketing_footer current_user={assigns[:current_user]} />
</div>
